{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-exponential-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-exponential-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the $q$-exponential grouplike","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-exponential"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-q-exponential-exists"],"tags":["existence","q-exponential","grouplike","hopf-algebra"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QExponential.exists_in_shuffle_hopf","text":"q-exponential-exists.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:q-exponential-exists\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}_q</code> be the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-shuffle Hopf algebra over a base ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> in which the Jackson integers <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[n]_q</code> are invertible. There exists a unique grouplike <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q \\in G(\\mathcal{H}_q)</code> satisfying <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">D_q \\exp_q = \\exp_q</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\epsilon(\\exp_q) = 1</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exponential-exists.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.22.3"}
